    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "History",
            "paragraphs": [
                "St Sepulchre has a long and rich history, with a worshipping community here since at least 1137, a medieval shell and tower that survived the great fire of London and a classical interior. There are many historical figures associated with the site, including John Rogers (1505-55) bible translator executed under the reign of Mary I, Captain John Smith (1579-1631), one of the founders of Jamestown, Virginia and Sir Henry Wood (1869-1944), founder of the ‘Proms’. There are also green spaces within the Benefice including the Garden of Remembrance and Postman’s Park, and drinking fountains."
            ]
        }
